Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?X8:=20static=20verifier=20=E2=80=94=2022=20refu?=
 =?UTF-8?q?sal=20codes,=20100=20golden=20mutants,=206/6=20NC?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

aura_exec::verify is a pure function over bytes: verify(&bytes, &VerifyLimits)
-> Report. No engine, no execution, no new crate, no new dependency.

- 22 stable refusal codes, each with a witness (unit test and/or golden
  mutant); Report carries functions/instructions/peak stack/peak body and one
  Problem { code, offset, detail } per defect, the offset pointing into the
  module.
- tools/gen_x8_mutants.py: an independent Python section walker that damages
  one thing per module and states the expected verdict — 15 kinds x 6 over the
  six shipped artifacts plus a second round for five kinds = 100 mutants.
- Depth checks: section framing/order, function<->code counts, value types,
  locals, import whitelist (+ restrictive config), globals, memory maximum,
  run export, and per body the instruction/local budgets, operand-stack depth
  with callee signatures from the type section, label depth and the
  local/global/call/call_indirect index spaces.
- Measured: 100/100 mutants refused with the expected code, 0 mismatches; 6/6
  shipped artifacts accepted (peak stack 7, peak body 630 instructions).
- tools/nc_x8.py: 6 negative controls, each reddening a named test after a
  green baseline. 37 tests in the gate, 359 in the workspace, 159 NC,
  4826 vectors across 26 fixtures, 239 external crates unchanged.
- Fixed: call read no callee signature (store.wasm was refused and every stack
  number was fiction); body offsets were relative to the body slice.
